    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-5068",
      "problem": "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of the ellipse given below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14275040/assets/287ac4f6deaad8076bccd5f6ad4e8d80f26d60f3ab96d94b220c12dd09f00abd.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The major axis is the longest diameter of the ellipse, which is the line segment bounded by the points $(-3,1)$ and $(7,1).$ So, the length of the major axis is $7 - (-3) = 10.$\n\nThe minor axis is the shortest diameter of the ellipse, which is the line segment bounded by the points $(2,-1)$ and $(2,3).$ So, the length of the minor axis is $3 - (-1) = 4.$",
